# Testing & Quality

- Cover: env validation, ticket hash/consume, replay/expiry, concurrent GETDEL, Origin allow/deny/missing, malformed/duplicate tickets, frame size limits, connection limits, heartbeat timeout, max lifetime, log redaction, graceful shutdown, Redis-down fail-closed.
- Unit tests inject fake clocks, ticket stores, and Redis. Integration tests may use real Redis when available; skip clearly when not.
- Never use real production credentials or live external SaaS in tests.
- CI must run `lint`, `typecheck`, `test`, and `build`. Docker smoke (`compose config`, health endpoints) when the runner allows.
- Never claim green results unless the commands were actually executed and passed. Distinguish pre-existing sibling-repo failures from new realtime failures.
- Prefer Vitest. Keep tests deterministic; avoid timing flakes by injecting intervals/timeouts.

```ts
// ✅ Assert single-use redemption
await store.consume(ticket); // ok
await expect(store.consume(ticket)).rejects.toBeInstanceOf(TicketRejectedError);
```
